From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:45:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vhost: leave virtio-gpu blob memory out of the vhost
 memory table

A host-visible blob that virtio-gpu maps into the guest is a RAM region,
so every blob that came or went changed the vhost memory table, and each
vhost device then rebuilt it in the kernel from the main loop with the
BQL held. On the Raspberry Pi 4 that was two holds of 345 and 282 ms
when a Venus context was created during a 720p60 video in a WebView, and
an ALSA under-run. No vhost device reads or writes GPU blob memory.

Measured with a build of the same change that also logged its timings.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 hw/virtio/vhost.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/virtio/vhost.c b/hw/virtio/vhost.c
index 74e53a066..bad45efdf 100644
--- a/hw/virtio/vhost.c
+++ b/hw/virtio/vhost.c
@@ -664,6 +664,24 @@ static bool vhost_section(struct vhost_dev *dev, MemoryRegionSection *section)
 {
     MemoryRegion *mr = section->mr;
 
+    /*
+     * q11-100: leave virtio-gpu blob memory out of the vhost memory table.
+     *
+     * WHY. A host-visible blob that virtio-gpu maps into the guest is a RAM
+     * region, so every blob that comes or goes changed the table, and each
+     * vhost device (vhost-net, vhost-vsock) then rebuilt it in the kernel
+     * (VHOST_SET_MEM_TABLE) from the main loop with the BQL held. Measured on
+     * the Raspberry Pi 4 during WebView 720p60 in the HMI: when a Venus context
+     * was created, two holds of 345 and 282 ms, almost all kernel time, next to
+     * the "vhost_set_memory" lines, and an ALSA under-run. No vhost device
+     * reads or writes GPU blob memory: its buffers are in guest RAM.
+     */
+    if (mr->owner &&
+        object_dynamic_cast(mr->owner, "virtio-gpu-virgl-hostmem-region")) {
+        trace_vhost_reject_section(mr->name, 4);
+        return false;
+    }
+
     if (memory_region_is_ram(mr) && !memory_region_is_rom(mr)) {
         uint8_t dirty_mask = memory_region_get_dirty_log_mask(mr);
         uint8_t handled_dirty;
